Additional Use Grant: There are two ways to use the Licensed Work in production
                      without a commercial licence. Section 1 is about the
                      repositories You review. Section 2 is about You. Meeting
                      EITHER is enough.

                      1. PUBLIC REPOSITORIES — ALWAYS FREE. You may make
                      production use of the Licensed Work on any repository
                      whose source code is publicly readable, without
                      authentication and without payment, by anyone. There is no
                      limit of any kind on this use: not on the number of
                      repositories, pipeline runs, findings or contributors, and
                      not on the size of Your organisation. A trillion-dollar
                      company reviewing its open-source projects with the
                      Licensed Work needs nothing from the Licensor.

                      Repository visibility is assessed when the Licensed Work
                      runs. A repository that is made private stops qualifying
                      under this section from that point, and falls to section 2.

                      2. SMALL ORGANISATIONS — PRIVATE REPOSITORIES TOO. For
                      repositories that are not public, You may make production
                      use of the Licensed Work within Your own software
                      development lifecycle — including continuous integration,
                      code review and release engineering — for so long as BOTH
                      of the following are true:

                        (a) the total annual gross revenue of You and Your
                            Affiliates, for Your most recently completed fiscal
                            year, is less than USD $5,000,000; and

                        (b) no more than 10 individuals in total contribute
                            source code to the non-public repositories the
                            Licensed Work reviews for You.

                      "Affiliates" means any entity that controls, is controlled
                      by, or is under common control with You. Revenue is
                      counted across the whole group, so a small team inside a
                      larger organisation is measured by that organisation.

                      Limb (b) counts contributors to the REPOSITORIES REVIEWED,
                      not Your own headcount. This is deliberate and it is what
                      makes section 3 self-executing: pointing the Licensed Work
                      at a large private codebase exceeds it, whoever You are.

                      If either limb ceases to be true, this grant ends for Your
                      non-public repositories and a commercial licence is
                      required to continue. Contact licensing@reyse.ai.

                      3. WHOSE CODE. Within the limits above it does not matter
                      whose source code You review. Running the Licensed Work on
                      code You are contractually engaged to develop or secure —
                      as a consultancy, a contractor or a managed service
                      provider — is permitted on the same terms as running it on
                      Your own. The line drawn here is size, not client
                      relationship.

                      4. NOT AS A SERVICE. You may not make the functionality of
                      the Licensed Work available to third parties as a hosted,
                      managed or embedded service, whether or not for a fee.
                      This prohibits offering the Licensed Work ITSELF to others
                      to run; it does not prohibit using the Licensed Work to
                      perform Your own work, which section 3 permits.

                      5. MODIFICATIONS COME BACK. If You modify the Licensed
                      Work and make production use of the modified version, You
                      must EITHER:

                        (a) make the source of Your modifications publicly
                            available, at no charge, under this same License,
                            within 90 days of that use beginning; OR

                        (b) obtain a commercial licence, which permits You to
                            keep Your modifications private. Contact
                            licensing@reyse.ai.

                      Under (a) You are not required to contribute anything to
                      the Licensor, to open a pull request, or to support what
                      You publish — only to publish it, so that anyone who
                      received the Licensed Work can also receive Your
                      improvements to it.

                      This obligation covers changes to the Licensed Work
                      itself. It does NOT cover Your own source code, Your
                      configuration, Your entry points, Your benign controls,
                      Your findings, or any work that merely invokes the
                      Licensed Work. Reviewing Your code with the Licensed Work
                      never obliges You to publish that code.

                      6. WHAT THIS DOES NOT ASK OF YOU. You supply Your own
                      model inference; nothing in this License requires You to
                      send code, findings or telemetry to the Licensor, and the
                      Licensed Work is built so that You do not.

